IMPORT prelude

-- Gas Act 2001 (Singapore) -- whether my gas and I are within the Act, whether I need a gas licence, who may do gas work for me and
-- whom I may engage, getting connected and what I can be charged, who pays to repair, move or remove the pipes on my land, building
-- over a pipe, digging near one, damaging one, my meter, when my supply can be cut off and what gets it back, how much notice I get
-- before the gas companies enter, the safety rules on the job, my liability for my company's offence, and the most I can be fined.
--
-- SEAT: the gas consumer -- the owner or occupier of premises supplied with piped gas -- and, with them, any member of the public the
-- Act's prohibitions reach in the same everyday way: a person who engages gas work, digs near a gas pipe or handles a meter. Never
-- the Authority, a gas licensee or a court.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 2 ("consumer", "gas", "gas service work", "earthworks", "occupier"); s 6(1), (2), (6); ss 11, 12(6), 13;
-- s 22(1), (2), (4), (5); s 23; s 29(1), (2); s 30(2) to (4); s 31; s 32(1) to (3), (5) to (9); ss 32A(1), (4), (5), 32B; s 39;
-- s 44(1), (3), (4); s 46(1) to (3), (5); s 47(1), (2), (4); s 49; s 50(1), (5); s 52; ss 53, 54, 55(2), 56, 58, 59, 60(1)(a);
-- s 61(4); s 64; s 89; s 91; s 92.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 September 2025 (amendments to Act 27 of 2024
-- shown), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GA2001.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: administration and the Authority's information powers (ss 3 to 5); the grant, conditions, transfer, modification,
-- revocation and enforcement of gas licences (ss 7 to 10, 12(1) to (5), Part 4); the transporter's network duties, prices, works,
-- tree-felling and special administration (ss 21, 24 to 28, 33 to 36); inspection responsibility prescribed by Gazette order
-- (s 29(3) to (6)); retailers' duties, prices and access, gas allocation and key facilities (ss 37, 38 to 38C, 43A, 45); the false
-- statement and impersonation offences beyond their penalty (ss 40 to 42); distress (s 43); the scheme for valuing gas taken
-- (s 48); disconnection under ss 39(2), 44(2), 47(5), 51 and 67 beyond what s 52 says about getting supply back; the rest of the
-- entry procedure and compensation for damage on entry (ss 60(1)(b) to (6), 61(1) to (3), (5)); the gas importer provisions
-- (ss 61AA, 61AB); the Gas Network Code, codes of practice and directions (Parts 7, 7A); control of designated licensees (Part 7B);
-- the transporter's escape duties (ss 65, 66, 68); severe gas shortage (Part 8A); competition (Part 9); the Appeal Panel and appeals
-- (Part 10, s 93); exemptions, service, regulations and transitional provisions (ss 94 to 101). No regulations, Gazette orders or
-- exemptions under the Act were deposited, so the gazetted dates in s 6(1), s 8 exemptions, the classes of gas service work
-- (s 12(5)), the offences prescribed as compoundable (s 92(2)) and the penalties for offences created by regulations are asked as
-- facts or answered NOTHING, as each decision says.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the individual's seat, with the
-- design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC USE AS
-- ADVICE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Gas Act 2001 -- the gas consumer`

§§ `s 2 -- is my gas within the Act, and am I a consumer`

-- s 2: "gas" means "natural gas and town gas, but does not include liquefied petroleum gas".
-- "consumer" means a person "(a) to whose premises gas is shipped; or (b) whose premises are connected to a gas pipeline network for
-- the purpose of obtaining a supply of gas".
DECLARE `Kind of gas` IS ONE OF
    `piped natural gas`                       -- "natural gas"
    `town gas`                                -- "town gas"
    `liquefied petroleum gas`                 -- LPG, e.g. a cylinder: excluded by s 2

DECLARE `My supply` HAS
    `the kind of gas`                                                  IS A `Kind of gas`
    `gas is shipped to my premises`                                    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2 "consumer" (a)
    `my premises are connected to a gas pipeline network to get gas`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2 "consumer" (b)

GIVEN `my supply` IS A `My supply`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my gas gas within the Act` IF
    CONSIDER `my supply`'s `the kind of gas`
    WHEN `liquefied petroleum gas` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `my supply` IS A `My supply`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a consumer` IF
        `Is my gas gas within the Act` `my supply`
    AND (   `my supply`'s `gas is shipped to my premises`
         OR `my supply`'s `my premises are connected to a gas pipeline network to get gas`)

§§ `s 6 -- do I need a gas licence for what I do`

-- s 6(1): "no person may" (a) convey gas through a gas pipeline or network "to any premises"; (b) convey gas for a gas transporter
-- "(other than as an employee of the gas transporter)"; (c) ship gas, (d) retail gas and (g) produce town gas "on or after such date
-- as the Minister may, by order in the Gazette, specify"; (e), (f) operate an onshore receiving facility or LNG terminal; (ga), (h)
-- import natural gas or LNG; "unless the person is authorised to do so by a gas licence or is exempted under section 8".
-- s 6(2): "A person may, without a licence -- (a) convey, in any premises or part thereof in which that person has an interest, gas
-- supplied for use in the premises; or (b) sell, for use in any premises or part thereof in which that person has an interest, gas
-- retailed for use in the premises by a gas retailer."
-- No Gazette order or s 8 exemption was deposited: whether the Minister's date has passed, and whether I am exempted, are asked.
DECLARE `Gas activity` IS ONE OF
    `conveying gas within premises I have an interest in`                       -- s 6(2)(a)
    `reselling retailed gas for use in premises I have an interest in`          -- s 6(2)(b), e.g. a landlord to tenants
    `conveying gas through a pipeline to other premises`                        -- s 6(1)(a)
    `conveying gas for a gas transporter as its employee`                       -- s 6(1)(b), excepted
    `conveying gas for a gas transporter as a contractor`                       -- s 6(1)(b)
    `shipping gas`                                                              -- s 6(1)(c)
    `retailing gas`                                                             -- s 6(1)(d)
    `producing town gas`                                                        -- s 6(1)(g)
    `importing natural gas or LNG`                                              -- s 6(1)(ga), (h)

DECLARE `My activity` HAS
    `what I do`                                       IS A `Gas activity`
    `the Minister's gazetted date has passed`         IS A BOOLEAN    -- s 6(1)(c), (d), (g) only
    `I hold a gas licence for it`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am exempted under section 8`                   IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `my activity` IS A `My activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I need a gas licence for what I do` IF
    CONSIDER `my activity`'s `what I do`
    WHEN `conveying gas within premises I have an interest in` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `reselling retailed gas for use in premises I have an interest in` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `conveying gas for a gas transporter as its employee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `shipping gas` THEN `my activity`'s `the Minister's gazetted date has passed`
    WHEN `retailing gas` THEN `my activity`'s `the Minister's gazetted date has passed`
    WHEN `producing town gas` THEN `my activity`'s `the Minister's gazetted date has passed`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 6(6): a contravention of (1) is an offence; the penalty is in the penalty table below.
GIVEN `my activity` IS A `My activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by doing it without a licence` IF
        `Do I need a gas licence for what I do` `my activity`
    AND NOT `my activity`'s `I hold a gas licence for it`
    AND NOT `my activity`'s `I am exempted under section 8`

§§ `ss 11 to 13 -- who may do gas work for me, and whom I may engage`

-- s 2: "gas service work" means "any work carried out on any gas installation or gas appliance, in whole or in part, including any
-- design, construction, installation, commissioning, erection, testing, repair, addition, alteration or maintenance work".
-- s 11(1): no person may carry out gas service work "unless he or she is registered as a professional engineer and has a valid
-- practising certificate under the Professional Engineers Act 1991, or holds a valid gas service worker licence in respect of the
-- specific class of work". (3): the section "does not apply to a gas transporter, a gas transport agent, or an employee" of either.
-- s 12(6): a holder of a Public Utilities Act licence in force immediately before 14 February 2008 is, "unless the Authority directs
-- otherwise, deemed to be a licensed gas service worker".
-- s 13: "Any person who employs or instructs any person who is not a licensed gas service worker to carry out or cause to be carried
-- out any gas service work shall be guilty of an offence."
-- The classes of work are set by the Authority (s 12(5)); none was deposited, so whether a licence covers this class is asked.
DECLARE `My gas worker` HAS
    `is a registered professional engineer with a valid practising certificate`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a gas service worker licence for this class of work`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a gas service worker licence for another class only`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `held a Public Utilities Act gas service worker licence before 14 February 2008` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Authority has directed otherwise for that old licence`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a gas transporter, a gas transport agent or an employee of one`            IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the worker` IS A `My gas worker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my worker a licensed gas service worker` IF
        `the worker`'s `holds a gas service worker licence for this class of work`
    OR  `the worker`'s `holds a gas service worker licence for another class only`
    OR  (    `the worker`'s `held a Public Utilities Act gas service worker licence before 14 February 2008`
         AND NOT `the worker`'s `the Authority has directed otherwise for that old licence`)

GIVEN `the worker` IS A `My gas worker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my worker carry out my gas service work` IF
        `the worker`'s `is a registered professional engineer with a valid practising certificate`
    OR  `the worker`'s `holds a gas service worker licence for this class of work`
    OR  `the worker`'s `is a gas transporter, a gas transport agent or an employee of one`

-- s 13 follows its words: "a licensed gas service worker", with no carve-out for the engineer or the transporter's employee whom
-- s 11 lets do the work, and no reference to the class. This is the literal reading; no case law was searched.
GIVEN `the worker` IS A `My gas worker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by engaging my worker` IF
    NOT `Is my worker a licensed gas service worker` `the worker`

§§ `ss 22 and 23 -- getting my premises connected`

-- s 22(1): a gas transporter "must, on the request of the owner or occupier of any premises", install a gas service isolation valve,
-- lay a gas service pipe "and connect such premises to the relevant gas main". (2): the costs "may only be recovered ... to the
-- extent that the costs have not been previously recovered from any other person". (4): nothing requires it to connect "if (a) the
-- gas transporter is unable to do so by circumstances beyond its control; or (b) ... doing so, would involve a danger to the public".
-- (5): where a new or increased supply needs a new or enlarged gas main or other works, it "may refuse ... until" the owner or
-- occupier "enters into an agreement ... for the payment of a reasonable amount". s 23: it may require "reasonable security" and,
-- if it is not given or "has become invalid or insufficient", refuse "for so long as the failure or insufficiency continues".
-- s 2 "occupier" "does not include a lodger"; whether I am the owner or occupier is asked.
DECLARE `My connection request` HAS
    `I am the owner or occupier of the premises`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transporter is unable to connect by circumstances beyond its control`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `connecting would involve a danger to the public`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `a new or enlarged gas main or other works is needed for the supply`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have agreed to pay a reasonable amount for those works`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transporter has required security`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have given valid and sufficient security`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cost of the valve, the service pipe and the connection`                IS A NUMBER
    `the part of that cost already recovered from others`                       IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `my request` IS A `My connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the gas transporter connect my premises` IF
        `my request`'s `I am the owner or occupier of the premises`
    AND NOT `my request`'s `the transporter is unable to connect by circumstances beyond its control`
    AND NOT `my request`'s `connecting would involve a danger to the public`
    AND (   NOT `my request`'s `a new or enlarged gas main or other works is needed for the supply`
         OR `my request`'s `I have agreed to pay a reasonable amount for those works`)
    AND (   NOT `my request`'s `the transporter has required security`
         OR `my request`'s `I have given valid and sufficient security`)

GIVEN `my request` IS A `My connection request`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be charged for the connection` IS
    IF `my request`'s `the part of that cost already recovered from others` AT LEAST `my request`'s `the cost of the valve, the service pipe and the connection`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `my request`'s `the cost of the valve, the service pipe and the connection` MINUS `my request`'s `the part of that cost already recovered from others`

§§ `ss 29 to 31 -- the pipes on my land`

-- s 29(1): the gas transporter "must carry out any necessary work of maintenance, repair or renewal" of the gas service pipe up to
-- the gas service isolation valve, and the valve. (2): the cost is paid "(a) in the case of work made necessary by any intentional
-- or negligent act of the consumer, by the consumer if the gas transporter requires the consumer to pay; (b) in any other case, by
-- the gas transporter".
DECLARE `Who pays` IS ONE OF
    `I pay`
    `the gas transporter pays`
    `I pay to the extent I benefit, the gas transporter pays the rest`

GIVEN `my intentional or negligent act made the work necessary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the gas transporter requires me to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who pays`
DECIDE `Who pays to repair my gas service pipe` IS
    IF `my intentional or negligent act made the work necessary` AND `the gas transporter requires me to pay`
    THEN `I pay`
    ELSE `the gas transporter pays`

-- s 30(2): the transporter "must, at the request of the owner or occupier ..., relocate the gas service pipe if it is satisfied that
-- such relocation is reasonable and the owner or occupier complies with such terms and conditions as the gas transporter may impose,
-- including ... payment ... of all reasonable costs". The duty names only the gas service pipe; a gas main may be asked about under
-- (1) but (2) does not oblige. The transporter's satisfaction is its judgment: an input.
GIVEN `it is a gas service pipe, not a gas main` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the gas transporter is satisfied the relocation is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I comply with its terms, including paying the reasonable costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the gas transporter move the pipe for me` IF
        `it is a gas service pipe, not a gas main`
    AND `the gas transporter is satisfied the relocation is reasonable`
    AND `I comply with its terms, including paying the reasonable costs`

-- s 30(3): a gas main or service pipe "no longer in use by the occupier or any other person for the purposes of the supply of gas, or
-- by the gas transporter for the conveyance of gas" -- the transporter "must at the reasonable request of the owner, remove [it] ...
-- at its own expense". (4): "owner" includes "any person having a leasehold interest with an unexpired term of not less than 7 years".
-- Whether the request is "reasonable" is not decided here; it is taken as made reasonably.
GIVEN `the pipe is still in use` IS A BOOLEAN, `I own the freehold` IS A BOOLEAN, `years left on my lease` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I make the transporter remove the disused pipe at its own expense` IF
        NOT `the pipe is still in use`
    AND (`I own the freehold` OR `years left on my lease` AT LEAST 7)

-- s 31(1): "No person may build, erect or construct anything over any existing gas transmission pipeline, gas main or gas service pipe
-- ... without the approval of the gas transporter." (4): an offence. (2): an owner or occupier with a structure over a gas main or
-- service pipe "must have [it] relocated or diverted away". (3): costs fall "(a) on the owner or occupier to the extent that the
-- owner or occupier benefits ..., or where the building or structure was built ... by the owner or occupier in contravention of
-- subsection (1); and (b) by the gas transporter in all other circumstances".
GIVEN `I built over the pipe` IS A BOOLEAN, `the gas transporter approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by building over the pipe` IF
    `I built over the pipe` AND NOT `the gas transporter approved it`

GIVEN `I built it without the transporter's approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `I benefit from the diversion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who pays`
DECIDE `Who pays to divert the pipe from under my building` IS
    IF `I built it without the transporter's approval`
    THEN `I pay`
    ELSE IF `I benefit from the diversion`
         THEN `I pay to the extent I benefit, the gas transporter pays the rest`
         ELSE `the gas transporter pays`

§§ `s 32 -- digging near a gas pipe`

-- s 2 "earthworks": excavating; work in or under the ground for building, roads, mains, cables or soil investigation; boring,
-- dredging, jacking, levelling, piling or tunnelling by mechanical means; "the driving or sinking of any bar, rod, pole, picket,
-- casing or tube into the ground". Whether the work is earthworks, and "within the vicinity" (not defined), are asked.
-- s 32(1): no person may commence or carry out earthworks within the vicinity of a transporter's gas plant or pipe "unless the person
-- (a) has given to the gas transporter not less than 7 days' notice in writing ...; (b) has obtained ... the necessary information on
-- the location ...; and (c) has consulted the gas transporter on the steps to be taken to prevent [damage]". (2): "The Authority
-- may, if it thinks fit in any particular case, modify the period". (3): duties while working: (a) comply with "all reasonable
-- requirements of the gas transporter"; (b) "ensure that reasonable precautions are taken"; (c) "allow the gas transporter
-- reasonable access". (5): (1) does not stop earthworks where the person "has reasonable cause to believe that it is necessary to do
-- so in the interest of public or private safety"; (6) who "must, as soon as practicable but not more than 24 hours after the
-- earthworks have been commenced", give written notice. (7): contravening (1), (3) or (6) is an offence.
-- (8), (9): the defence -- "all reasonable steps" or "all reasonable precautions and ... all due diligence" -- but where it "involves
-- acting on information supplied by" the gas transporter (or an owner of infrastructure housing a transmission pipeline, s 32(10)),
-- it may not be relied on "without permission of the court" unless written notice identifying the supplier was served on the
-- prosecutor "within 14 clear days before the hearing". Read as: served at least 14 clear days before.
DECLARE `My earthworks` HAS
    `they are earthworks within the vicinity of a transporter's gas plant or pipe`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of written notice I gave the transporter`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the period the Authority set for my case`                                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- s 32(2); NOTHING if not modified
    `I obtained the location of the gas plant or pipe`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I consulted the transporter on preventing damage`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had reasonable cause to believe they were necessary for safety`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours after starting that I gave written notice`                               IS A NUMBER         -- s 32(6), safety case
    `I complied with the transporter's reasonable requirements`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I ensured reasonable precautions were taken`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I allowed the transporter reasonable access`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I can prove reasonable steps or due diligence`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `my defence relies on information from the gas transporter`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `clear days before the hearing I served notice on the prosecutor`               IS A NUMBER
    `the court has given permission`                                                IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `my works` IS A `My earthworks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days' notice must I give before digging` IS
    CONSIDER `my works`'s `the period the Authority set for my case`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 7
    WHEN JUST `days` THEN `days`

GIVEN `my works` IS A `My earthworks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I start the earthworks` IF
        NOT `my works`'s `they are earthworks within the vicinity of a transporter's gas plant or pipe`
    OR  `my works`'s `I had reasonable cause to believe they were necessary for safety`
    OR  (    `my works`'s `days of written notice I gave the transporter` AT LEAST `How many days' notice must I give before digging` `my works`
         AND `my works`'s `I obtained the location of the gas plant or pipe`
         AND `my works`'s `I consulted the transporter on preventing damage`)

GIVEN `my works` IS A `My earthworks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I contravened section 32` IF
    `my works`'s `they are earthworks within the vicinity of a transporter's gas plant or pipe`
    AND (   NOT `May I start the earthworks` `my works`                                         -- s 32(1)
         OR NOT `my works`'s `I complied with the transporter's reasonable requirements`        -- s 32(3)(a)
         OR NOT `my works`'s `I ensured reasonable precautions were taken`                      -- s 32(3)(b)
         OR NOT `my works`'s `I allowed the transporter reasonable access`                      -- s 32(3)(c)
         OR (    `my works`'s `I had reasonable cause to believe they were necessary for safety`  -- s 32(6)
             AND `my works`'s `hours after starting that I gave written notice` GREATER THAN 24))

GIVEN `I can prove reasonable steps or due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `my defence relies on information from the gas transporter` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `clear days before the hearing I served notice on the prosecutor` IS A NUMBER,
      `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I rely on the due diligence defence` IF
        `I can prove reasonable steps or due diligence`
    AND (   NOT `my defence relies on information from the gas transporter`
         OR `clear days before the hearing I served notice on the prosecutor` AT LEAST 14
         OR `the court has given permission`)

GIVEN `my works` IS A `My earthworks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of the earthworks offence` IF
        `Have I contravened section 32` `my works`
    AND NOT `Can I rely on the due diligence defence`
                (`my works`'s `I can prove reasonable steps or due diligence`)
                (`my works`'s `my defence relies on information from the gas transporter`)
                (`my works`'s `clear days before the hearing I served notice on the prosecutor`)
                (`my works`'s `the court has given permission`)

-- The s 32(6) duty as a regulative rule: after starting safety earthworks without notice, written notice within 24 hours.
DECLARE `Party to safety earthworks` IS ONE OF `the person who started the earthworks`
DECLARE `Step after safety earthworks` IS ONE OF `give the transporter written notice of the nature and extent of the earthworks`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to safety earthworks` `Step after safety earthworks`
DECIDE `my duty to notify after safety earthworks` IS
    PARTY `the person who started the earthworks`
    MUST `give the transporter written notice of the nature and extent of the earthworks`
    WITHIN 24
    LEST BREACH BY `the person who started the earthworks`

§§ `ss 32A and 32B -- damaging a gas pipe`

-- s 32A(1): any person who "(a) removes, destroys or damages any gas plant or gas pipe which is part of a gas pipeline network" of a
-- gas licensee; "(b) causes or permits" that; or "(c) in any way other than by paragraph (a) or (b), wilfully or recklessly hinders or
-- prevents" its use, is guilty of an offence. (a) and (b) state no mental element. (4): for (a) or (b) only, the defence of "all
-- reasonable precautions and ... all due diligence"; (5) subject to the same 14-clear-day notice as s 32(9) -- answered by
-- `Can I rely on the due diligence defence` and given here as a fact.
-- s 32B: any person who "wilfully, recklessly or negligently -- (a) does any act, or permits or causes any act to be done, which
-- damages or is likely to damage" a submarine gas pipeline in Singapore's territorial waters (or its housing), or "(b) omits to do
-- anything required to prevent any damage". No defence is stated.
DECLARE `Pipe damaged` IS ONE OF
    `a gas pipe in a licensee's network on land`
    `a submarine gas pipeline in Singapore's territorial waters`

DECLARE `What I did` IS ONE OF
    `I removed, destroyed or damaged it`
    `I caused or permitted its removal, destruction or damage`
    `I otherwise hindered or prevented its use`
    `I did something likely to damage it`
    `I omitted to do something required to prevent damage`

DECLARE `My state of mind` IS ONE OF
    `without fault`
    `negligently`
    `recklessly`
    `wilfully`

DECLARE `The damage` HAS
    `the pipe`                                IS A `Pipe damaged`
    `what I did`                              IS A `What I did`
    `my state of mind`                        IS A `My state of mind`
    `I can rely on the due diligence defence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the damage` IS A `The damage`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by what I did to the gas pipe` IS
    CONSIDER `the damage`'s `the pipe`
    WHEN `a gas pipe in a licensee's network on land` THEN
        CONSIDER `the damage`'s `what I did`
        WHEN `I removed, destroyed or damaged it` THEN NOT `the damage`'s `I can rely on the due diligence defence`
        WHEN `I caused or permitted its removal, destruction or damage` THEN NOT `the damage`'s `I can rely on the due diligence defence`
        WHEN `I otherwise hindered or prevented its use` THEN `wilful or reckless` (`the damage`'s `my state of mind`)
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `a submarine gas pipeline in Singapore's territorial waters` THEN
        CONSIDER `the damage`'s `my state of mind`
        WHEN `without fault` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHERE
        GIVEN `the state` IS A `My state of mind`
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `wilful or reckless` `the state` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the state`
            WHEN `wilfully` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `recklessly` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 39 and 44 -- reporting damage, and my meter`

-- s 39(1): where a gas pipeline, internal pipe or other apparatus on premises "becomes obstructed or in any way damaged, the occupier
-- of the premises must, immediately on the obstruction or damage coming to the occupier's knowledge, give notice thereof" to the gas
-- transporter, relevant gas shipper or relevant gas retailer. (2): an occupier "who neglects to give notice ... after acquiring such
-- knowledge" commits an offence (no penalty stated, so s 91), and the supply may be cut until repairs are done.
GIVEN `I am the occupier` IS A BOOLEAN, `I knew of the obstruction or damage` IS A BOOLEAN, `I gave notice immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by not reporting the damaged pipe` IF
    `I am the occupier` AND `I knew of the obstruction or damage` AND NOT `I gave notice immediately`

-- s 44(1): "Every consumer must take the consumer's supply of gas through a meter". (3): a meter owned by the transporter or the
-- relevant gas shipper and "lent or hired to a consumer" must be kept by it "at all times and without charge to that consumer ... in
-- proper order". (4): "A consumer must at all times keep a meter which belongs to the consumer in proper order".
DECLARE `Whose meter` IS ONE OF
    `my own meter`
    `a meter lent or hired to me by the gas transporter or gas shipper`

DECLARE `Who keeps the meter` IS ONE OF
    `I must keep it in proper order`
    `the gas transporter or gas shipper must keep it in proper order, without charge to me`

GIVEN `the meter` IS A `Whose meter`
GIVETH A `Who keeps the meter`
DECIDE `Who must keep my meter in proper order` IS
    CONSIDER `the meter`
    WHEN `my own meter` THEN `I must keep it in proper order`
    WHEN `a meter lent or hired to me by the gas transporter or gas shipper` THEN `the gas transporter or gas shipper must keep it in proper order, without charge to me`

§§ `s 46 -- can my retailer cut me off for an unpaid bill`

-- s 46(1): where "(a) a demand in writing is made by a gas retailer for the payment of any of the charges due ... and (b) the consumer
-- does not pay those charges within 28 days after the making of the demand"; (2) or a written request for "a deposit by way of
-- reasonable security" is not met "within 7 days after the making of the request"; (3) "If the gas retailer is a relevant gas
-- retailer, it may, after giving not less than 7 days' notice of its intention -- (a) discontinue the supply" and recover the
-- expenses. (4): an assignee relevant gas retailer may do the same. (5): "not exercisable in respect of any charges or deposit the
-- amount of which is genuinely in dispute".
DECLARE `My unpaid bill` HAS
    `the retailer demanded payment in writing`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I did not pay within 28 days after the demand`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the retailer asked in writing for a deposit as security`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I did not give the deposit within 7 days after the request`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is my relevant gas retailer, or has the right by assignment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of notice of its intention to cut off my supply`            IS A NUMBER
    `the amount is genuinely in dispute`                              IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `my bill` IS A `My unpaid bill`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my gas retailer cut off my supply for non-payment` IF
        (   (`my bill`'s `the retailer demanded payment in writing` AND `my bill`'s `I did not pay within 28 days after the demand`)
         OR (`my bill`'s `the retailer asked in writing for a deposit as security` AND `my bill`'s `I did not give the deposit within 7 days after the request`))
    AND `my bill`'s `it is my relevant gas retailer, or has the right by assignment`
    AND `my bill`'s `days of notice of its intention to cut off my supply` AT LEAST 7
    AND NOT `my bill`'s `the amount is genuinely in dispute`

§§ `ss 47, 49 and 50 -- meter tampering, reconnecting, and connecting a meter`

-- s 47(1): offences of (a) intentionally laying a pipe or gas fitting to connect with a transporter's network "without the consent of
-- the gas transporter"; (b) "dishonestly or fraudulently" abstracting, using, consuming or diverting gas; (c) altering or tampering
-- with a meter or meter installation; (d) anything that "compromises or adversely affects" its proper operation; (e) causing or
-- permitting (b) to (d).
-- s 47(4): a person is "presumed, until the contrary is proved" to have tampered with a meter if it is proved that at the time (a)(i)
-- a device was attached to or near it "for the purpose of altering the index" or preventing it registering; (ii) the covering "had a
-- hole which is not a result of ordinary wear and tear"; (iii) a seal or lock fastened by a gas licensee was "damaged, removed or
-- changed"; or (iv) a licensee's paint or chemical compound was "damaged or removed or altered"; "and (b) that the person had, at the
-- time of the alleged conduct, custody or control of the meter".
GIVEN `a device was attached to or near the meter to alter or stop its registering` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the meter cover had a hole not from ordinary wear and tear` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a licensee's seal or lock on the meter was damaged, removed or changed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a licensee's paint or chemical marking was damaged, removed or altered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I had custody or control of the meter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be presumed to have tampered with the meter` IF
        (   `a device was attached to or near the meter to alter or stop its registering`
         OR `the meter cover had a hole not from ordinary wear and tear`
         OR `a licensee's seal or lock on the meter was damaged, removed or changed`
         OR `a licensee's paint or chemical marking was damaged, removed or altered`)
    AND `I had custody or control of the meter`

-- s 49(1): where premises "have been disconnected by a gas transporter in exercise of the powers under this Act or pursuant to a valid
-- and enforceable contractual right", any person who "without the consent of the gas transporter, re-connects" commits an offence;
-- (2) the same for a supply discontinued by a gas shipper or gas retailer.
GIVEN `my supply was cut off under the Act or a valid contractual right` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I reconnected or restored it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the company that cut it off consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by reconnecting my supply` IF
    `my supply was cut off under the Act or a valid contractual right` AND `I reconnected or restored it` AND NOT `the company that cut it off consented`

-- s 50(1): no person may connect a meter or internal pipe to a gas pipeline, or disconnect it, "unless the person has given 48 hours'
-- notice in the prescribed form ... (c) in a case where gas is supplied to the premises by a relevant gas shipper or relevant gas
-- retailer, to the gas shipper or gas retailer; and (d) in any other case, to the gas transporter". The prescribed form is not
-- deposited; giving notice in it is taken as given.
DECLARE `Notice recipient` IS ONE OF
    `my gas shipper or gas retailer`
    `the gas transporter`

GIVEN `my gas is supplied by a relevant gas shipper or gas retailer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice recipient`
DECIDE `Whom must I notify before connecting or disconnecting a meter` IS
    IF `my gas is supplied by a relevant gas shipper or gas retailer` THEN `my gas shipper or gas retailer` ELSE `the gas transporter`

GIVEN `my gas is supplied by a relevant gas shipper or gas retailer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `whom I notified` IS A `Notice recipient`,
      `hours of notice I gave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I connect or disconnect the meter or internal pipe` IF
        `whom I notified` EQUALS `Whom must I notify before connecting or disconnecting a meter` `my gas is supplied by a relevant gas shipper or gas retailer`
    AND `hours of notice I gave` AT LEAST 48

§§ `s 52 -- getting my supply back`

-- s 52(2): after a disconnection or discontinuance under the Act, the gas company is "not under any obligation" to reconnect or
-- restore "until -- (a) the consumer is no longer the owner or occupier of the premises; or (b) the consumer -- (i) has made good the
-- default, or remedied the matter ...; and (ii) has paid the reasonable expenses of disconnecting and re-connecting".
-- The section lifts the bar; it does not itself impose a duty to reconnect (s 22(3) may). Read as: the bar is lifted.
GIVEN `I am no longer the owner or occupier` IS A BOOLEAN, `I have made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I have paid the reasonable expenses of cutting off and reconnecting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done what section 52 requires before my supply comes back` IF
        `I am no longer the owner or occupier`
    OR  (`I have made good the default` AND `I have paid the reasonable expenses of cutting off and reconnecting`)

§§ `ss 53 to 60 -- notice before the gas companies enter my premises`

-- s 53: on reasonable cause to suspect an escape, an authorised person "may immediately and without notice enter".
-- ss 55(2), 58(1), 59: entry to cut off or remove a meter, to replace, repair or alter pipes, or to survey, "after 7 days' notice to
-- the occupier ... or to the owner of the premises if they are unoccupied". s 58(2): in an emergency from a defect, "immediately and
-- without notice", with notice and the justification "as soon as possible" afterwards.
-- ss 54, 56: entry to read the meter, inspect fittings, or check for an unauthorised reconnection is "Subject to section 60", which
-- gives no particular period; s 60(1)(a): "where no particular requirement is made, 14 days' notice of the intended entry". Read as
-- 14 days. Regulations may provide otherwise (s 61(5)); none was deposited.
DECLARE `Purpose of entry` IS ONE OF
    `a suspected gas escape`                                         -- s 53
    `reading the meter or inspecting fittings during supply`         -- s 54
    `cutting off the supply or removing a meter`                     -- s 55
    `checking whether I reconnected without consent`                 -- s 56
    `replacing, repairing or altering pipes or fittings`             -- s 58(1)
    `an emergency from a defect in gas plant or a fitting`           -- s 58(2)
    `surveying whether my premises suit the transporter's activities` -- s 59

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `Purpose of entry`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days' notice must I be given before they enter` IS
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `a suspected gas escape` THEN 0
    WHEN `an emergency from a defect in gas plant or a fitting` THEN 0
    WHEN `cutting off the supply or removing a meter` THEN 7
    WHEN `replacing, repairing or altering pipes or fittings` THEN 7
    WHEN `surveying whether my premises suit the transporter's activities` THEN 7
    OTHERWISE 14

§§ `s 64 -- safety on the job`

-- s 64(2): "No person may connect a gas installation to a source of gas without ensuring that every outlet is sealed with the
-- appropriate gas fitting and the gas installation has been tested for gas tightness."
-- (5): no one exposing a part that "contains or contained flammable gas may smoke or use any source of ignition unless the gas
-- installation has been purged ... or has otherwise been made safe". (6): no one "searching for an escape of gas ... may use any
-- source of ignition unless [it] is incorporated as part of an instrument designed for the detection of gas". (7): "No person may use
-- any naked flame or carry out any hotwork in the vicinity where gas is known to be leaking." No exception to (7).
GIVEN `every outlet is sealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the installation was tested for gas tightness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I connect the gas installation to the gas` IF
    `every outlet is sealed` AND `the installation was tested for gas tightness`

DECLARE `Ignition situation` IS ONE OF
    `working on an exposed part of a gas installation`
    `searching for a gas escape`
    `near a known gas leak`

GIVEN `the situation` IS A `Ignition situation`, `the installation was purged or made safe` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the ignition is part of a gas detector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I use a flame or other source of ignition` IF
    CONSIDER `the situation`
    WHEN `working on an exposed part of a gas installation` THEN `the installation was purged or made safe`
    WHEN `searching for a gas escape` THEN `the ignition is part of a gas detector`
    WHEN `near a known gas leak` THEN FALSE

§§ `s 89 -- my company's offence`

-- s 89: where a company, firm, society or other body commits an offence, a person who was "a director, manager, secretary or other
-- similar officer or a partner ... or was purporting to act in any such capacity, shall be guilty of that offence ... unless the person
-- proves that (a) the offence was committed without the person's consent or connivance; and (b) the person had exercised all such
-- due diligence". Both limbs must be proved.
GIVEN `my company committed an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `I was an officer or partner, or purported to act as one` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I prove it was without my consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `I prove I exercised all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of my company's offence` IF
        `my company committed an offence under the Act`
    AND `I was an officer or partner, or purported to act as one`
    AND NOT (`I prove it was without my consent or connivance` AND `I prove I exercised all due diligence`)

§§ `Penalties and composition -- what I can be made to pay`

-- s 6(6): "$1 million and, in the case of a continuing offence, ... $25,000 for every day or part of a day" -- no imprisonment.
-- s 32(7): "$100,000 or ... 5 years or ... both". s 32A(1): "$1 million or ... 5 years". s 32B: "$2 million or ... 5 years".
-- s 47(2): "a fine that is the total of -- (i) an amount not exceeding $50,000; and (ii) an amount equal to 3 times the value of gas",
-- or 5 years, "and, in the case of a continuing offence, ... $250 for every day". s 49: "$10,000 or ... 3 years". s 50(5): "$5,000".
-- s 61(4): intentionally obstructing entry, "$10,000 or ... 12 months", or "where the obstruction endangers life or property,
-- ... $50,000 or ... 5 years". s 64(8): "$50,000 or ... 5 years", "$250 for every day".
-- s 91: "Any person guilty of an offence under this Act for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- "$10,000 or ... 12 months or
-- ... both and, in the case of a continuing offence, ... $250 for every day or part of a day" (ss 11, 13, 31, 39, 40, 41, 42).
-- An offence created by regulations under s 96 carries what the regulations set; none was deposited, so NOTHING.
DECLARE `My offence` IS ONE OF
    `doing a licensable gas activity without a licence`              -- s 6(6)
    `doing gas service work without being qualified`                 -- s 11, s 91
    `engaging an unlicensed gas service worker`                      -- s 13, s 91
    `building over a gas pipe without approval`                      -- s 31(4), s 91
    `an earthworks offence`                                          -- s 32(7)
    `damaging a gas pipe on land`                                    -- s 32A(1)
    `damaging a submarine gas pipeline`                              -- s 32B
    `not reporting a damaged pipe`                                   -- s 39(2), s 91
    `meter tampering or taking gas`                                  -- s 47(2)
    `reconnecting without consent`                                   -- s 49
    `connecting a meter without notice`                              -- s 50(5)
    `obstructing entry`                                              -- s 61(4)
    `obstructing entry so as to endanger life or property`           -- s 61(4)
    `breaking a gas safety rule`                                     -- s 64(8)
    `an offence created by regulations`                              -- s 96: not deposited

DECLARE `Maximum punishment` HAS
    `fine in dollars`                    IS A NUMBER
    `months in prison`                   IS A NUMBER    -- 0: no imprisonment; where both are given, "or to both"
    `further fine per day continuing`    IS A NUMBER    -- after conviction; 0 where none is provided

GIVEN `fine` IS A NUMBER, `months` IS A NUMBER, `daily` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum punishment`
`up to` MEANS JUST (`Maximum punishment` WITH `fine in dollars` IS `fine`, `months in prison` IS `months`, `further fine per day continuing` IS `daily`)

-- s 47(3): the value "may be determined based on the amount of such gas fairly and reasonably estimated"; the value is asked.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`, `the value of the gas taken or supplied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum punishment`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be punished with` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `doing a licensable gas activity without a licence` THEN `up to` 1000000 0 25000
    WHEN `an earthworks offence` THEN `up to` 100000 60 0
    WHEN `damaging a gas pipe on land` THEN `up to` 1000000 60 0
    WHEN `damaging a submarine gas pipeline` THEN `up to` 2000000 60 0
    WHEN `meter tampering or taking gas` THEN `up to` (50000 PLUS 3 TIMES `the value of the gas taken or supplied`) 60 250
    WHEN `reconnecting without consent` THEN `up to` 10000 36 0
    WHEN `connecting a meter without notice` THEN `up to` 5000 0 0
    WHEN `obstructing entry` THEN `up to` 10000 12 0
    WHEN `obstructing entry so as to endanger life or property` THEN `up to` 50000 60 0
    WHEN `breaking a gas safety rule` THEN `up to` 50000 60 250
    WHEN `an offence created by regulations` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE `up to` 10000 12 250

-- s 92(1): the Authority "may, in its discretion, compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a compoundable offence by
-- collecting ... a sum not exceeding $3,000". (2): the offences are prescribed by regulations, not deposited; asked. NOTHING means my
-- offence cannot be compounded. Whether the Authority offers to compound is its discretion and is not decided here.
GIVEN `the regulations make my offence compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be asked to pay to compound my offence` IS
    IF `the regulations make my offence compoundable` THEN JUST 3000 ELSE NOTHING
